"<div><div class=\" response-message\"></div></div><div><div class=\" response-message\"><h2>State Transitions</h2>\n<p>✅ Transition analysis complete</p>\n<p>This transition analysis defines the logic governing movement between the states of the <strong>User Authentication Flow</strong>. It ensures that security invariants are maintained (e.g., no one reaches &quot;Logged In&quot; without passing &quot;Validating&quot;) and that error paths are clearly defined.</p>\n<h3>User Authentication State Transition Table</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr><th align=\"left\">Source State</th><th align=\"left\">Event / Trigger</th><th align=\"left\">Target State</th><th align=\"left\">Guard Conditions</th><th align=\"left\">Actions</th><th align=\"left\">Priority</th></tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Submit Credentials</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating Primary Credentials</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Input fields are non-empty and sanitized.</td><td align=\"left\">Initialize login attempt session; Start timer.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Validation Success</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>MFA Challenge Pending</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Credentials match AND MFA is enabled for user.</td><td align=\"left\">Generate MFA challenge (SMS/TOTP); Send challenge.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Validation Success</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Password Reset Required</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Credentials match AND <code>force_reset</code> flag is TRUE.</td><td align=\"left\">Generate temporary restricted token.</td><td align=\"left\">2</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Validation Success</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged In</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Credentials match AND MFA is NOT enabled AND Reset NOT required.</td><td align=\"left\">Create full Session Token; Log successful login.</td><td align=\"left\">3</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Validation Failure</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Account Locked</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Credentials mismatch AND <code>fail_count</code> + 1 &gt;= <code>max_threshold</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Set <code>is_locked</code> = true; Log security event; Notify user.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Validation Failure</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Authentication Failed</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Credentials mismatch AND <code>fail_count</code> + 1 &lt; <code>max_threshold</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Increment <code>fail_count</code>; Log failed attempt.</td><td align=\"left\">2</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating</strong></td><td align=\"left\">System Error</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Identity Provider or DB is unreachable.</td><td align=\"left\">Display &quot;Service Unavailable&quot; message; Clear transient data.</td><td align=\"left\">3</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>MFA Pending</strong></td><td align=\"left\">MFA Success</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged In</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Provided token is valid AND NOT expired.</td><td align=\"left\">Upgrade session to &quot;Full Access&quot;; Reset <code>fail_count</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>MFA Pending</strong></td><td align=\"left\">MFA Failure</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Authentication Failed</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Provided token is invalid AND <code>mfa_fail_count</code> &lt; <code>max_mfa_tries</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Increment <code>mfa_fail_count</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>MFA Pending</strong></td><td align=\"left\">MFA Failure</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Account Locked</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><code>mfa_fail_count</code> + 1 &gt;= <code>max_mfa_tries</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Set <code>is_locked</code> = true; Revoke partial session.</td><td align=\"left\">2</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>MFA Pending</strong></td><td align=\"left\">MFA Timeout</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Session Expired</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><code>current_time</code> &gt; <code>mfa_window_expiry</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Revoke partial session; Log timeout.</td><td align=\"left\">3</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged In</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Logout</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">User clicks &quot;Logout&quot; or API call received.</td><td align=\"left\">Revoke Session Token; Clear server-side cache.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged In</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Session Timeout</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Session Expired</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><code>idle_time</code> &gt; <code>max_idle</code> OR <code>total_time</code> &gt; <code>absolute_timeout</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Revoke Session Token.</td><td align=\"left\">2</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged In</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Admin Action</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Account Suspended</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Admin sets status to &quot;Suspended&quot; or &quot;Disabled&quot;.</td><td align=\"left\">Immediate revocation of all active tokens for User ID.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Authentication Failed</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Retry Login</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Validating Primary Credentials</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><code>is_locked</code> is FALSE.</td><td align=\"left\">Clear previous error messages.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Authentication Failed</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Abandon / Timeout</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">No user activity for X minutes.</td><td align=\"left\">Clear transient attempt data.</td><td align=\"left\">2</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Account Locked</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Cool-down Expired</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\"><code>current_time</code> &gt; <code>lockout_expiry_time</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Reset <code>fail_count</code>; Set <code>is_locked</code> = false.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Account Locked</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Admin Unlock</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Admin manually clears lock via dashboard.</td><td align=\"left\">Reset <code>fail_count</code>; Set <code>is_locked</code> = false.</td><td align=\"left\">2</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Password Reset Required</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Update Success</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged In</strong></td><td align=\"left\">New password meets complexity policy.</td><td align=\"left\">Update DB with new hash; Clear <code>force_reset</code> flag.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Password Reset Required</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Logout / Cancel</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">User abandons flow.</td><td align=\"left\">Revoke restricted token.</td><td align=\"left\">2</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Session Expired</strong></td><td align=\"left\">System Redirect</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Client detects 401 Unauthorized or local timeout.</td><td align=\"left\">Clear client-side cookies/storage; Redirect to Login.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n<tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Account Suspended</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Admin Reinstatement</td><td align=\"left\"><strong>Logged Out</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Admin sets status to &quot;Active&quot;.</td><td align=\"left\">Update user status; Notify user via email.</td><td align=\"left\">1</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<h3>Detailed Transition Logic Analysis</h3>\n<h4>1. The &quot;Happy Path&quot; (Standard Authentication)</h4>\n<p>The most common flow is <strong>Logged Out</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Validating</strong> $\\rightarrow$ <strong>Logged In</strong>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Guard Check:</strong> The transition from Validating to Logged In is the most critical security gate. It must ensure that MFA is not required and no administrative flags (like a forced reset) are present.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>2. The Security Escalation (Lockout Logic)</h4>\n<p>Transitions to <strong>Account Locked</strong> can occur from both <strong>Validating</strong> (primary password failure) and <strong>MFA Challenge Pending</strong> (secondary factor failure).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Action:</strong> Upon entering the Locked state, the system must not only change the database flag but also ensure any existing partial sessions (from the MFA stage) are immediately destroyed.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>3. The Intermediary Constraint (Password Reset)</h4>\n<p>The <strong>Password Reset Required</strong> state acts as a &quot;jail&quot; state.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Invariant Maintenance:</strong> While in this state, the user is technically &quot;authenticated&quot; (we know who they are), but the transition to <strong>Logged In</strong> is strictly guarded by the &quot;Update Success&quot; event. No other navigation to protected resources is permitted.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>4. Session Lifecycle (Expiration &amp; Revocation)</h4>\n<p><strong>Session Expired</strong> is a transient error state.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Recovery:</strong> It almost always leads back to <strong>Logged Out</strong>. This transition is often automated by middleware that detects an expired JWT or session cookie, performing the &quot;Action&quot; of clearing local storage before the user even realizes the state change has occurred.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>5. Administrative Overrides</h4>\n<p>The <strong>Account Suspended</strong> state is unique because it can be triggered as an external event (Admin Action) while the user is in the <strong>Logged In</strong> state.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Priority:</strong> This transition has the highest priority; it must bypass normal user activity and force an immediate exit from the stable &quot;Logged In&quot; state to protect the system.</li>\n</ul>\n</div></div><div><div class=\"spinner-border\" role=\"status\"><span class=\"sr-only\">Loading...</span></div></div>"